  "status": "blocked",
  "statusRationale": "The public JSON proof endpoint and browser proof route declare no-store cache policy, and PR #240 moved the route source from static Netlify deploy artifacts to repo-owned Netlify Function responses. Current provider evidence now shows Netlify Durable bypass and Netlify Edge miss on canonical proof/control routes while Cloudflare reports dynamic handling, but Netlify still emits low nonzero Age on dynamic no-store responses. Provider and CDN headers are recorded as evidence only and are not semantic authority; the existing proof still blocks because nonzero Age contradicts the declared no-store evidence boundary. Future static, API-like, and app route classes are classified but not claimed as staging-ready.",
  "blocksStagingSpecificEnablement": true,
